    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "f5cvt",
      "x": 3001,
      "y": 95,
      "width": 696,
      "height": 1602,
      "content": "Trip Quest Project summary\n\nHow it works:\nMultiplayer\nEach user has an account — user sets their preferences which the AI uses to cater missions\nCan create groups — per trip\nAI then compiles missions/games per player and a overall mission for the group\nTake pictures and/or just mark missions as complete\nPoints and Badges (custom passport)\n\n\nGamification angle/how to gain points:\ncompleting missions successfully\nfirst to finish a mission amongst friends gets most points (friendly competition)\nfriends can rank each other's missions (like best tasting food or best image taken or funniest experience etc)\n\n\nLater versions:\nStrangers could see trips and ask to join the trip and be a “travel player”\nDifferent groups travelling to the same destination could have a competition for the “Best travel group” especially during peak seasons\n\n\nPossible monetization strats:\nBusinesses paying to get ranked and first preference\nBattle passes for users (users buy passes which gives them discounts to some locations but we have to chat with business providers)\n\n\nSmall business impact:\nsmall businesses get included in missions for exposure\neach mission checkpoint will have each business tagged in the image (2nd level of exposure)\napp might have a \"travel feed\" page which shares users checkpoint images with the businesses tagged (3rd level of exposure)"
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "id": "wfxE9",
      "x": 3001,
      "y": 1161,
      "width": 696,
      "height": 1602,
      "content": "For the hackathon MVP, build these 9 screens:\n1. Welcome / Sign in\nIntroduces Trip Quest and lets users:\nCreate an account or continue as a guest\nEnter their name\nStart a new trip or join an existing one\nKeep this lightweight. Do not overbuild authentication.\n2. Trips Dashboard\nShows the user’s trips.\nEach trip card should display:\nDestination\nDates\nGroup members\nCurrent leaderboard position\n“Continue trip” button\nPrimary actions: Create trip and Join trip.\n3. Create or Join Trip\nUse one screen with two clear paths:\nCreate a trip by entering destination, dates, and trip name\nJoin a trip using an invite code\nAfter creation, generate an invite code or share link.\n4. Trip Lobby\nThe group’s starting point before missions are generated.\nIt should show:\nDestination and trip dates\nGroup members\nInvite code\nEach player’s selected interests\n“Generate missions” button\nThis is where the group sees that the AI is building a personalised game.\n5. Player Preferences\nEach player selects interests such as:\nFood\nHistory\nNature\nPhotography\nShopping\nAdventure\nLocal culture\nNightlife\nThey can also choose a difficulty or personality style, such as relaxed, adventurous, competitive, or creative.\nThe AI uses this information to create better missions.\n6. Mission Board\nThis is the main screen during the trip.\nSeparate missions into:\nMy missions\nGroup mission\nCompleted\nEach mission card should show:\nMission title\nShort description\nPoints available\nTime limit, if relevant\nCompletion status\nExample: “Find the best local snack and convince your group to try it.”\n7. Mission Detail / Submit Proof\nShows the full mission instructions.\nPlayers can:\nView hints\nSee the points available\nTake or upload a photo\nAdd a short description\nMark the mission complete\nFor the demo, photo upload and a completion button are enough.\n8. Voting / Mission Results\nAfter a player submits a mission, friends can vote or react.\nShow:\nThe submitted photo or story\nThe player’s name\nVoting categories such as funniest, best photo, or most creative\nVote buttons\nPoints awarded\nThis is the key social screen because friends judge each other’s experiences.\n9. Leaderboard / Passport\nCombine these into one screen with two tabs:\nLeaderboard\nPlayer rankings\nTotal points\nMissions completed\nBadges earned\n“First to finish” bonus\nPassport\nCompleted destinations\nEarned badges\nFavourite mission types\nBest photos or achievements\nThe leaderboard proves the competition. The passport gives players a personal record of the trip.\nThe demo flow\nBuild the product around this path:\nCreate trip → invite friends → choose interests → generate missions → complete a mission → vote → leaderboard updates\nDo not build separate screens yet for strangers joining, business promotion, battle passes, or a travel feed. Those can be shown as future ideas, not part of the working prototype."
    },
